---
layout: layout.njk
# A single, fixed address for every certificate ever issued -- unlike
# `event.njk`'s own per-edition permalink (D-19), a certificate names no
# event this page could key a per-page address off. `tools/convener_ops/
# certificate.py`'s own `VERIFICATION_BASE` is pinned against this literal
# by `tools/tests/test_workflows.py::
# test_certificate_verification_base_matches_the_verify_page_permalink` --
# change both together.
permalink: "/verify/"
pageTitle: "Verify a certificate"
eleventyComputed:
  # See `archives.njk` for why this is computed rather than a plain
  # front-matter string.
  pageDescription: "Confirm an attendance certificate issued by {{ site.organisation }}, using the identifier printed on it -- no account needed."
---

<section class="hero">
  {# The charter's motif, the same one the home page's hero draws -- see
     src/_data/motif.json and tools/scripts/generate_motif.py. #}
  <svg class="hero__motif" viewBox="{{ motif.view_box }}" fill="none" stroke-width="{{ motif.stroke_width }}" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="{{ motif.path }}"/>
  </svg>

  <div class="container hero__inner">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Certificate of attendance</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">Check a certificate.</h1>
    <p class="hero__lede">
      Follow the link or scan the code printed on a certificate issued by {{ site.organisation }} to confirm
      it here &mdash; entirely offline, with no account, and without sending us anything but
      the identifier already printed on it.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section container">
  {#
    The verification island itself, mounted here -- extracted from
    the operators' application into its own small, self-contained bundle,
    the same move registration made (`event.njk`'s own
    `#registration-form`). A visitor checking a certificate never
    downloads the operators' cockpit to read four lines back.

    `#verify-app` is `app/src/islands/verify/main.tsx`'s own `MOUNT_ID`.
    Unlike `#registration-form`, this element carries no `data-*`
    attribute: one static page serves every certificate ever issued, and
    what varies between visits is the URL's own fragment (the identifier
    and, when present, the token `certificate.verification_url` appends
    after `#/`) -- `main.tsx` reads that directly from `location.hash`,
    never from this markup. The element starts empty; `verify.js` fills it
    in, which is exactly why the `<noscript>` fallback beside it exists --
    without JavaScript, nothing here would ever render at all, and this
    page has no static text worth showing in its place (the answer
    genuinely depends on the fragment JavaScript alone can read).
  #}
  <div id="verify-app" class="verify"></div>
  <noscript>
    <p class="notice">
      Checking a certificate needs JavaScript enabled. If you cannot enable it, write to
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact }}">{{ site.contact }}</a> with the
      certificate identifier and we will check it by hand.
    </p>
  </noscript>
  <script type="module" src="{{ '/app/islands/verify/verify.js' | url }}"></script>
</section>
